{"base_rate":0.3018292682926829,"brier":0.17735365853658536,"bss":0.15837783953067808,"bss_hi":0.26580518833045896,"bss_lo":0.025456420314894035,"chart":{"base":[322.9,202.8],"fp":[184.5,147.9],"lead":"62,307.5 272,308.6 482,306.3 692,304","note":{"base":"skill 0.16 — higher than 24% of cities","fp":"low end -2pp, high end +25pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.6 °C — better than 99% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 1%; promised 95% → rained 67%"},"rel":"73.9,462.1 137.3,427.8 294.1,375.1 508,251.7 658.2,174.9"},"country":"KI","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1466463414634146,"ess":370.0260105244362,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tarawa</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tarawa rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>74%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 656 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 20.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.16, ranked 165 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(118&ndash;189) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>41</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>63%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 10 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tarawa</b> <span class=\"muted\">Kiribati</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;30% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 30% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.16</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>118&ndash;189\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>656 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tarawa &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tarawa\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-ancho