4545447,200.0 338.06622950819667,202.98360655737704 375.93625000000003,165.875 407.7424324324324,111.45945945945948\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 41 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.2590243902439\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"68.41771428571428\" cy=\"376.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"86.52823529411765\" cy=\"339.1764705882353\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"112.22025316455694\" cy=\"358.9620253164557\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 28%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"157.7540298507463\" cy=\"316.80597014925377\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 46%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"219.4990909090909\" cy=\"293.75757575757575\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 63%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"281.39545454545447\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 79%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"338.06622950819667\" cy=\"202.98360655737704\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"375.93625000000003\" cy=\"165.875\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.7424324324324\" cy=\"111.45945945945948\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(30%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Tarawa the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.29) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.08).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>-0.083</td><td class='num'>15.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>-0.082</td><td class='num'>19.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>165</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.151</td><td class='num'>14.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>147</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.287</td><td class='num'>6.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":1.3278,"lon":172.97696,"n":656,"n_cities":216,"name":"Tarawa","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0007317073170731707,"n":41,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.02942857142857143,"n":70,"obs":0.014285714285714285,"sig":false},{"hi":0.12,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.08058823529411765,"n":68,"obs":0.11764705882352941,"sig":false},{"hi":0.22,"lo":0.12,"mean":0.15316455696202527,"n":79,"obs":0.06329113924050633,"sig":true},{"hi":0.37,"lo":0.22,"mean":0.28179104477611944,"n":67,"obs":0.1791044776119403,"sig":false},{"hi":0.55,"lo":0.37,"mean":0.4562121212121212,"n":66,"obs":0.24242424242424243,"sig":true},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.55,"mean":0.6310606060606059,"n":66,"obs":0.5,"sig":true},{"hi":0.86,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.7911475409836064,"n":61,"obs":0.4918032786885246,"sig":true},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.86,"mean":0.8981250000000001,"n":64,"obs":0.59375,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9879729729729729,"n":74,"obs":0.7432432432432432,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":20.2,"provisional":false,"rank":165,"rank_hi":189.0,"rank_lo":118.0,"reliability":0.03267008278968324,"resolution":0.06437917851873558,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"tarawa","station":"","timezone":"Pacific/Tarawa"}